# Sanity Studio — copy to `.env`. Hosting setup: root `README.md` → "Deploy".
#
# PUBLIC: the Studio build inlines every `SANITY_STUDIO_*` variable into its JS bundle, and
# `sanity build` / `sanity deploy` refuse to run with a `SANITY_STUDIO_*` token, secret or
# password set (`sanity.cli.ts`). The SECRET values below use plain names.

# Required. Same project id as `web/.env.local`.
SANITY_STUDIO_PROJECT_ID=

# Dataset to edit. Empty = auto-select (root README → "How `@repo/sanity-dataset-resolve`
# picks a dataset"). On the Netlify Studio site, `studio/netlify.toml` sets it per deploy context.
SANITY_STUDIO_DATASET=
# Order while the dataset is empty: `production`, `development`, `preview`, or a dataset
# name tried first (e.g. `staging`).
# SANITY_STUDIO_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=staging
# Only if your datasets aren't named `development` / `production`.
# SANITY_STUDIO_DATASET_DEVELOPMENT=development
# SANITY_STUDIO_DATASET_PRODUCTION=production

# Web origin Presentation opens — scheme, host and port (localhost ≠ 127.0.0.1).
SANITY_STUDIO_PREVIEW_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
# More web origins Presentation may load, comma-separated (e.g. deploy previews).
# SANITY_STUDIO_WEB_PREVIEW_ORIGINS=https://deploy-preview-42--your-site.netlify.app

# This Studio's public URL; `pnpm studio:register` registers it. Same value as
# `NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_STUDIO_URL` on the web app. On Netlify, empty = the site's domain.
SANITY_STUDIO_HOSTING_URL=
# Sanity Hosting only (`pnpm studio:deploy`): the app id the first deploy prints, so later
# deploys skip the hostname prompt. Per project — never copy a fork's value.
# SANITY_STUDIO_APP_ID=

# SECRET. Deploy token, on the Netlify Studio site only: production deploys then run
# `pnpm studio:register`. Locally, `sanity login` does the job.
# SANITY_AUTH_TOKEN=

# SECRET. One-off scripts (`studio/scripts/`).
# `pnpm mux:migrate-assets`: Mux API token (the Mux plugin keeps its own credentials).
# Formerly `SANITY_STUDIO_MUX_TOKEN_*` — rename them.
# MUX_TOKEN_ID=
# MUX_TOKEN_SECRET=
